==Trivia==
This card's Genetic Apex illustration is part of a narrative illustration with {{TCG ID|Genetic Apex|Oddish|11}}, {{TCG ID|Genetic Apex|Venonat|16}}, and the illustration rare {{TCG ID|Genetic Apex|Snorlax|250}} from the same set. In this illustration, Bellsprout can be seen by one of Snorlax's hands; the Snorlax card reveals that Bellsprout is stuck on [[Kanto]] {{rt|11|Kanto}}, with Snorlax blocking the way to {{rt|12|Kanto}}. Together, these cards form the "A Big Snorlax Nuisance" [[Genetic Apex (TCG Pocket)#Themed Collections|Themed Collection]]. Oddish, Venonat, and Bellsprout also have the same stats and an attack that does 20 damage for one {{e|Grass}} Energy.

===Origin===
*This card's shiny rare illustration features a {{Shiny}} {{p|Bellsprout}}.
*{{m|Vine Whip}} is a [[move]] in the [[Pokémon games]] that {{p|Bellsprout}} can learn.
*This card's [[Pokédex]] entry comes from {{g|X}}.

